 ### <a id="orcl-sec-005"></a>ORCL-SEC-005: JPY/USD shared dependency failsafe
 
 - Type: Security
-- Statement: The JPY/USD oracle is shared by every branch and has the widest blast radius. A JPY-leg failure must therefore not cause immediate terminal shutdown. Exactly one `JpyUsdRateProvider` is deployed and injected into every active source; inherited or duplicated per-feed state is prohibited because it cannot provide shared storage. The provider stores `lastGoodJpyRate` with the same response's `lastGoodJpyUpdatedAt`, and on first failure sets `jpyFrozenSince = min(block.timestamp, lastGoodJpyUpdatedAt + PRM-ORACLE-001)`. Every branch therefore receives the same frozen rate and onset. While the oracle remains unhealthy after `PRM-ORACLE-006`, expiry is latched before returning `failure=true`, so the signal remains available to every consumer during that outage. A later fresh response must remain readable even after expiry: it adopts the live rate, clears `jpyFrozenSince` and `jpyFreezeExpired`, and emits `JpyRateUnfrozen`. A branch that already observed expiry remains pinned at its branch-local `lastGoodPrice`; a branch still on `primary` resumes the recovered live rate. When a source is behind `PriceFeedProxy`, it catches the expected source-level BorrowerOperations caller-mismatch during the unhealthy expiry episode and returns `failure=true`; the registered Proxy performs shutdown in the same transaction. Collateral, peg-monitor, canonical-rate, and backing failures remain branch-local terminal failures and are evaluated before JPY fallback. Monitor the provider address/state/events (`JpyRateFrozen`, `JpyRateUnfrozen`, `JpyFreezeExpired`) externally and fail deployment/preflight if active sources reference different providers.
-- Verification: unit (cached-rate timestamp provenance, immediate shutdown for stale and invalid responses on the first call after the freeze limit elapses with no traffic, first-observation anchoring while the cached rate is fresh, fresh recovery before and after expiry, stale responses do not clear expiry, a later outage expires independently, already-shut branches remain pinned while branches that did not observe expiry resume, standard and sUSDS implementations), integration (Proxy path), fork (JPY/USD staleness), manual (heartbeat × N and weekend update history finalization)
